ensive (i.e., have a non-null COMM_REQ_ATTRIBUTE), with these statistics included for each subject in the result. Present the columns in the following order: subject code, subject title, department name, school name, rank within school, average total units, total units variance, total units standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), and number of Communication Intensive subjects. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1758\", \"name\": \"Math 2024 12-Unit Subjects Row Numbers and Unit Deviations Matched with 2019FA TIP Course-Material Offerings\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Textbook Material Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2024 with total units equal to 12 in the Mathematics department, show the department code, department name, subject code, subject number, subject title, total units, the row number within each department ordered by subject code, the deviation of each subject's total units from the average total units of all Mathematics subjects offered in 2024, the number of enrolled students, responsible faculty name, school name, and the dense rank over the department name ordered by department name for those subjects that also have course materials and were offered in the term '2019FA'. Sort the table by department name and subject title. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_1833\", \"name\": \"Math Letter-Graded Subject Rollup by Grade Type with Organization Room Area Stddev and DLC Name\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Facility Space Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each department and subject grade type where the subject is offered in the current academic year, is letter graded, and the department is Mathematics (Course 18), provide the number of subjects, the minimum total units, the school name, the department phone number, the organization name, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the areas of its rooms, and the department's DLC name, including subtotals for each department (the corresponding department field is 'SUBTOTAL') and a grand total across all departments (the corresponding department field is 'TOTAL'). Do not repeat the department if it is the same as the previous row. Only include organizations that have more than 5 rooms, are associated with a non-null DLC key, and are not the 'ADMISSIONS' department or the 'Political Science' department. Sort the table by department, grade type, and descending standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of room areas. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2151\", \"name\": \"Degree-Granting Department 2022 Unit Average-Variance with Political Science HGN Lecture Unit Maximums\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Department Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each department that grants degrees (excluding the Biology department), provide the department name, the average and variance of the total units for subjects offered by that department in the 2022 academic year, and, if the department is Political Science, also include for each HGN code the maximum number of lecture units among all subjects in the course catalog and the subject title from the subject offered table for subjects offered in the year 2012 with more than 2 lecture units, as well as the number of enrolled students for those subjects. List the results ordered by the variance of total units in descending order, and for Political Science, by the maximum lecture units in descending order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2158\", \"name\": \"Math 2022 TIP Subjects with Joint-Subject Flag and Letter-Graded Unit Range-Variance\", \"category\": \"Textbook Material and Subject Offering Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered in the 2022 academic year by a degree-granting department, specifically in the Department of Mathematics (Course 18) and excluding subjects offered by the Department of Physics, provide the subject ID, subject title, department name, the number of enrolled students, the total number of lecture units, and, for each subject, indicate whether it is also offered as a joint subject with another department. Additionally, show the range and variance of the total units for letter graded subjects offered this year in the Mathematics department. List the results in order of subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2398\", \"name\": \"Department Course Counts with Fall-Only Non-Summer Subject Average TIP Enrollment\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Department Analysis\", \"desc\": \"Show the department names, the corresponding SIS subject code, subject code descriptions, graduate level, the total number of courses per department, and the average number of enrolled students for each subject in the department, considering only subjects that are offered in the fall term and are not offered in the summer term. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_2924\", \"name\": \"Engineering Degree-Granting Course Subjects Above Department Average Total Units\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Department Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For degree-granting courses in the School of Engineering, show the course description, department name, subject title, and the subject's grade type description, but only include those courses where the total units for the subject exceed the average total units for that department. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3236\", \"name\": \"Engineering Catalog Subjects Row Numbers Matched with 2017JA TIP Enrollment Windows\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Textbook Material Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered by departments in the School of Engineering that are also offered in the term '2017JA', show the subject title, total units, department full name, the row number within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by subject title, number of enrolled students, offering department name, department full name for the term, subject code, subject code description, and the minimum number of enrolled students over each subject code group, ordered by subject title and subject code. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_3668\", \"name\": \"Engineering Catalog Subjects Row Numbers Matched with TIP Material Detail Enrollment Windows\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Textbook Material Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered by departments in the School of Engineering, show the subject title, total units, department full name, and assign row numbers within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by subject title. Additionally, for each matching course material detail, provide the material status key, term code, subject ID, ISBN, material key, the course number description, the offering department name, and the maximum number of enrolled students for each row considering the current row and the next 2 rows ordered by material key. The results should include the subject title, total units, department full name, window row number, material status key, term code, subject ID, ISBN, material key, course number description, offering department name, and the maximum number of enrolled students, in that order, for subjects and course materials where the subject title and department code match between the two datasets. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"metric_id\": \"dw_4602\", \"name\": \"Engineering Subjects with Unique Course Material Counts and TIP Material Detail Enrollment Windows\", \"category\": \"Course Catalog and Textbook Material Comprehensive Analysis\", \"desc\": \"Show the department full names, subject titles, total units, and the number of unique course materials per subject for subjects offered by departments in the School of Engineering. For each subject, also provide the material status key, term code