`IS_DEGREE_GRANTING='Y'` + catalog `ACADEMIC_YEAR=2022` + `DEPARTMENT_NAME <> 'Political Science'` SUPPORTED (dw_2151/dw_1474 idioms); STUDENT_DEPARTMENT NOT-SUPPORTED (no degree-granting flag).\n\n**3c. Wording-to-Field Anchoring:** \"offered in the current academic year\" lexically matches `IS_OFFERED_THIS_YEAR` (\"whether the subject is offered in the current academic year\" — column desc). \"letter graded\" matches `GRADE_TYPE` desc \"'L' = letter graded\". \"2022 academic year\" matches `ACADEMIC_YEAR` (column_concept_year_columns decision guide: \"Group by COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.ACADEMIC_YEAR when the question says 'academic year YYYY' for offerings\"). \"degree-granting departments\" matches `SIS_DEPARTMENT.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING`.\n\n**3d. Precedent Usage Evidence:** Same-shape precedent count for part 1: 1 exact (dw_1833) plus ≥4 partial Math letter-graded/offered-this-year metrics (dw_1427, dw_1692, dw_2158, dw_1471) — all on COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED. Precedents for 2022 degree-granting per-department catalog counts: 2 (dw_2151, dw_1049) — both on COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED + SIS_DEPARTMENT. Precedents for top-N-departments-excluding-Political-Science CTEs: 2 (dw_1474, dw_4234).\n\n## 4. Business Usage\nCOURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED is the canonical source for grading, unit-structure, and offering-flag analytics (61 dependent metrics). SIS_DEPARTMENT is the canonical degree-granting/school filter dimension. The conditional \"also provide\" pattern is realized in precedents (dw_1833, dw_1427, dw_2151) via LEFT JOIN of a secondary CTE, yielding NULL when the condition doesn't hold.\n\n## 5. Coverage Checklist\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED: semantic_get ✔, metrics_by_table ✔\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT: semantic_get ✔\n- SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY: semantic_get ✔\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS: semantic_get ✔\n- dw_1833, dw_1474, dw_4234, dw_1049, dw_2151: semantic_get ✔\n- concept_subject_offering_facts, concept_department_dimension, column_concept_total_units, column_concept_department_name, column_concept_year_columns: semantic_get ✔\n- Other Phase-1 search hits (SUBJECT_SUMMARY, SUBJECT_OFFERED, CIS/DRUPAL catalogs, STUDENT_DEPARTMENT, SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT, TIP/LIBRARY/IAP/facilities/HR/time entities): screened via returned descs; facilities/HR/IAP/moira/space/time entities discarded as completely unrelated to subject-offering question; catalog/department/offering alternatives covered above via concept comparison matrices.\n- mysql_query: attempted 6 times — all failed with server authentication error (1045 Access denied), so live verification was impossible; SQL is built verbatim from verified precedent metric SQL.\n\n## 6. Recommendation\n\n**6a.** Use COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED (measures: `SUBJECT_ID` count, `TOTAL_UNITS` min; filters: `IS_OFFERED_THIS_YEAR='Y'`, `GRADE_TYPE='L'`, `ACADEMIC_YEAR=2022`) joined to SIS_DEPARTMENT (`DEPARTMENT_CODE`; filters `DEPARTMENT_NAME='Mathematics'`, `DEPARTMENT_CODE='18'`, `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING='Y'`, `DEPARTMENT_NAME <> 'Political Science'`).\n\n**6b.** Two CTEs: (1) Math letter-graded current-year rollup grouped by DEPARTMENT_NAME, GRADE_TYPE (dw_1833 idiom); (2) top-10 departments by 2022 catalog subject count, degree-granting, excluding Political Science (dw_2151 + dw_1474 idioms, `ORDER BY count DESC LIMIT 10`). LEFT JOIN (2) onto (1) by DEPARTMENT_NAME so the 2022 count is NULL when Mathematics is not in the top 10. SELECT exactly: department name, grade type, subject count, min total units, 2022 subject count.\n\n**6c.** *Data*: only the catalog table physically carries GRADE_TYPE and IS_OFFERED_THIS_YEAR (column definitions retrieved); SIS_DEPARTMENT is the only lookup with IS_DEGREE_GRANTING. *Semantic-network*: concept decision guides route grading/offering-flag questions to the catalog table and year grouping to its ACADEMIC_YEAR; join path DEPARTMENT_CODE documented on both tables. *Business*: dw_1833 is a verbatim precedent for part 1; dw_2151/dw_1049/dw_1474 establish